# .gitignore — a list of path patterns Git will pretend don't exist.
#
# Anything matching a line below is "untracked": Git won't show it in
# `git status`, won't stage it, and won't commit it. The golden rule is:
# commit *source* (things a human wrote), never commit *generated* output
# (things a tool can recreate from that source). If a build can regenerate
# it, it does not belong in history.
#
# Pattern quick-reference (so the rules below read clearly):
#   foo/      -> a directory named foo, anywhere it appears
#   *.x       -> any file ending in .x
#   /foo      -> foo only at the repo root (the leading slash anchors it)
#   foo       -> foo anywhere in the tree

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Build output  (the big one)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `cmake -B build` dumps ~490 MB of CMake cache, Ninja files, object files,
# and the compiled .vst3/.au/.app bundles in here. All 100% regenerated by
# the build command — zero reason to track it, and it would bloat the repo
# enormously. We anchor with a leading slash because the build dir lives at
# Saturate/build, and we also ignore any stray `build/` elsewhere to be safe.
Saturate/build/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Local-only planning docs  (kept out of the public/interview repo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These two stay on disk locally but never get pushed:
#   plan.md                              -> the full personal build plan
#   project_franky_doesit_template.md    -> a Claude memory node (has tooling
#                                           frontmatter + session IDs in it)
# The committed repo gets a clean README.md instead.
/plan.md
/project_franky_doesit_template.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. macOS filesystem junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Finder drops these invisible metadata files into folders (icon positions,
# thumbnails). They have nothing to do with the project and just create noise
# in commits, so we ignore them everywhere in the tree.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Editor / IDE scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-machine editor settings and swap files — personal to whoever's editing,
# not part of the project. (.vscode/ is sometimes committed on purpose for
# shared settings; we leave it out for now to keep the repo tool-agnostic.)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
